// Your own copy of this file is Developer.xcconfig, next to it, and git
// never sees it. `xcodegen generate` (and npm run ios) creates it from this
// one when it is missing. Both settings are empty by default; a personal
// (free) Apple ID team needs the first to build for its own phone.
//
// Identifiers are unique across every Apple developer team. mn.basu.app and
// group.mn.basu.shared already belong to one, so another team cannot sign
// for them. A suffix of your own makes them yours:
//   mn.basu.app.yourname, mn.basu.app.yourname.widgets,
//   group.mn.basu.shared.yourname.
//
// BASU_ID_SUFFIX = .yourname
//
// Where a debug build on a real phone finds the API. `localhost` on a phone
// is the phone; use the Mac's address on the same Wi-Fi. In an xcconfig
// `//` starts a comment, so the URL is written with $() in the middle:
//
// BASU_API = http:/$()/192.168.1.20:3000
